# =============================================================================
# .gitignore for yaml Stata package
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LaTeX auxiliary files (sj-manuscript)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.log
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
!stata.toc
!src/stata.toc
*.lof
*.lot
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.pdfsync
*.dvi
*.ps
*.pp
*.pp1
*.tag
paper/*.pdf
!paper/*-v[0-9]*.pdf

# Keep the compiled PDF for review (optional - remove if you want to exclude)
*.pdf

# Reference copies for the R&R: author-authorized to commit. Some items carry
# publisher copyright (Nature, StataCorp); see paper/R&R/references/README.md
# for per-file provenance and licence.
#
# Deliberately NOT widened to R&R* like the rules below. Later rounds inherit a
# copy of this directory, and re-committing publisher-copyright PDFs once per
# round buys nothing: the R&R copy is the one covered by that authorization.
# Leave the duplicates on disk and untracked.
!paper/R&R/references/*.pdf

# Figure shipped with the R&R package: the revised manuscript includes
# figures/yaml_layers_bw.pdf, so it must be tracked for the driver to compile.
# R&R* so each round is covered: the R&R_2 copy was silently untracked under
# the blanket *.pdf rule, which would have left a fresh clone unable to build
# the paper. Note the compiled main-*.pdf is deliberately NOT excepted -- it
# is a build product, regenerated by compiling the tracked sources.
!paper/R&R*/latex/figures/*.pdf

# Response letter is a send-time attachment (not in the zip); track the exact
# PDF sent to the editor. Regenerate from response-letter.md with:
#   pandoc response-letter.md -o response-letter.pdf --pdf-engine=lualatex \
#     -V geometry:margin=1in -V fontsize=11pt -V colorlinks=true
!paper/R&R*/response-letter.pdf

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stata temporary/log files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.smcl
*.gph
*.dta
tests/*.log
tests/output/

# R&R example-run artifacts shipped in the SJ package (audit trail; the article's
# stlogs are taken verbatim from the log, so these are tracked for reproducibility).
# Placed AFTER the blanket *.dta / *.log rules so these exceptions win.
# R&R* so each round is covered -- these three files are inputs to
# make_resubmission.py, and without them a fresh clone cannot build the zip.
!paper/R&R*/examples/yaml_sj_article_examples.log
!paper/R&R*/examples/*.dta

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS generated files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor/IDE files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backup files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.backup
*.orig
*.old

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Temporary files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.temp
~$*
# Large test fixtures (download separately)
qa/fixtures/_wbopendata_indicators.yaml

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# QA fixtures (extracted from fixtures.zip on first run)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
qa/fixtures/*.yaml

# R&R staging run directory (generated; audit-trail files ship in the SJ package zip).
# R&R* so each round is covered. This directory holds copies of src/ that are
# resynced every round; tracking them would create a second source of truth that
# drifts from src/. What actually ships is the do/log pair, tracked under
# examples/ above.
paper/R&R*/package-run/
__pycache__/
